Falsifies `designware_ethernet::proofs::every_ring_offset_is_inside_the_region`.

The defect: the receive descriptor offset stops reducing its index modulo the ring, so a cursor
that ever ran past the ring addresses past the ring's page and into the transmit ring.

Expected to fail: the harness's first assertion, on any index of 256 or more.

diff --git a/crates/designware_ethernet/src/lib.rs b/crates/designware_ethernet/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/designware_ethernet/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_ethernet/src/lib.rs
@@ -171,3 +171,3 @@ pub mod layout {
     pub const fn rx_descriptor(i: u16) -> u64 {
-        RX_RING + (i % RX_ENTRIES) as u64 * DESCRIPTOR_BYTES
+        RX_RING + i as u64 * DESCRIPTOR_BYTES
     }
